< Test-time scaling trades tokens for accuracy through longer chains of thought, sampling and search \cite{wei2022chain,snell2024scaling,wu2024inference,alomrani2025budget}; our forcing resembles budget forcing \cite{muennighoff2025s1}. Work on overthinking \cite{chen2024overthinking}, length control \cite{aggarwal2025l1} and learned think-or-not decisions \cite{zhang2025adaptthink} asks when reasoning is needed, and \citet{wan2026shadowprice} allocate tokens across queries. Multiple-choice answers depend on option order \cite{zheng2024mcq,pezeshkpour2024order}, and stated reasoning need not determine the answer \cite{turpin2023unfaithful,lanham2023faithfulness}; we measure both inside traces of an economic decision, in dollars. Program-aided and tool-using models offload arithmetic \cite{schick2023toolformer,gao2023pal,chen2023pot}. LLM agents have been studied as auction bidders and economic actors \cite{chen2024aucarena,zhu2024synthetic,ahmed2026bazaar,raman2024steer,fish2025econevals,deng2024bargaining}, and \citet{artola2026games} model providers that compete through test-time compute.
