< For $\le$14B open reasoning models making a single-bidder, pay-your-bid bid-landscape decision under budgets up to 768 forced tokens, arithmetic is rarely what costs money. The traces usually compute and write down the right comparison, and the loss comes when the answer is chosen: models cut off mid-list answer against what they have written, and some complete traces answer by list position. In this setting a reader that takes the best of the values the trace states recovers most of what a calculator would, at no extra token cost.
