> For $\le$14B open reasoning models making a single-bidder, pay-your-bid bid-landscape decision under budgets up to 768 forced tokens, arithmetic costs money for one model only. The traces usually write down the right comparison; the loss comes when the answer is chosen, partly from answering before the list is finished and partly from answers that follow list position, and it shows up as overbidding that transfers surplus to sellers. An audit that compares the answer with the trace's own numbers catches most of these errors.
